# =====================================================================
# CyberForge ML service — manual test suite
# =====================================================================
# Target : Hugging Face Space  Che237/cyberforge  (Docker, FastAPI + Gradio)
#          https://che237-cyberforge.hf.space
# Tool   : VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
#          Click "Send Request" above any request; the response opens beside it.
#
# Token  : requests in section A read HF_TOKEN from ml-services/.env
#          (git-ignored) through {{$dotenv HF_TOKEN}}. The token is NOT in this
#          file. The Space itself is public, so sections B–O need no token.
#
# Waking : the Space sleeps after 48h idle. If A2 says "SLEEPING", send B1 and
#          wait ~20s; the first request wakes it. The chat model then loads in
#          the background for a minute or two (B1 shows local_llm.loaded).
#
# "Expect" lines are what the live Space returned on 2026-10-13 against Space
# commit c823c6a, with the four detection models retrained that day from
# public labelled data (see hf_space_deploy/trainer.py; each model's
# metadata.json in Che237/cyberforge-models holds its full training report).
# Scores from the trained models are deterministic, so they should match until
# the models are retrained again. Text from the chat model is generated and
# differs on every run.
#
# The models, briefly:
#   phishing_detection    39 features; decision point set for 2% false positives
#   malware_detection     39 features
#   web_attack_detection  22 payload features (SQL injection and XSS)
#   anomaly_detection     IsolationForest; its score is a margin, not a probability
# Two are in service by the owner's decision although they flag some well-known
# legitimate URLs; those cases are kept below as KNOWN FALSE POSITIVE (E7, E8).
# =====================================================================

@space = https://che237-cyberforge.hf.space
@hub = https://huggingface.co
@spaceId = Che237/cyberforge
@modelRepo = Che237/cyberforge-models
@hfToken = {{$dotenv HF_TOKEN}}
@json = application/json


# =====================================================================
# A. HUGGING FACE PLATFORM — token, Space runtime, model repo
# =====================================================================

### A1. Token is valid
# Expect: HTTP 200
# "name": "Che237", auth.accessToken.displayName "cyber", role "fineGrained".
# 401 means the token was revoked or .env is not being read.
# @name hfWhoami
GET {{hub}}/api/whoami-v2
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A2. Space runtime status
# Expect: HTTP 200
# "stage": "RUNNING", hardware.current "cpu-basic".
# Other stages: SLEEPING (send B1 to wake), BUILDING, RUNTIME_ERROR, PAUSED.
# @name spaceRuntime
GET {{hub}}/api/spaces/{{spaceId}}/runtime
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A3. Space metadata (sdk, last deploy time, commit)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# "sdk": "docker", "private": false, "lastModified" = last push to the Space.
# @name spaceInfo
GET {{hub}}/api/spaces/{{spaceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A4. Space secrets (names and update times only — values are never returned)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# Keys: GEMINI_API_KEY, GEMINI_MODEL, HF_TOKEN, HF_MODEL_REPO.
# The two GEMINI_* secrets are no longer read by the app and can be deleted.
# @name spaceSecrets
GET {{hub}}/api/spaces/{{spaceId}}/secrets
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A5. Model repo the Space downloads its .pkl files from
# Expect: HTTP 200
# "id": "Che237/cyberforge-models", "siblings" lists 30 files.
# @name modelRepoInfo
GET {{hub}}/api/models/{{modelRepo}}
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A6. Files for one model (the Space needs best_model.pkl + scaler.pkl)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# Swap the last path segment for malware_detection, anomaly_detection or
# web_attack_detection to check the others.
# @name modelRepoFiles
GET {{hub}}/api/models/{{modelRepo}}/tree/main/phishing_detection
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}

### A7. Restart the Space (DISRUPTIVE: ~1–2 min downtime, reloads all models)
# REST Client asks for confirmation before sending because of @note.
# Not run during verification, so there is no recorded result for this one.
# @note
# @name spaceRestart
POST {{hub}}/api/spaces/{{spaceId}}/restart
Authorization: Bearer {{hfToken}}


# =====================================================================
# B. HEALTH AND STATUS
# =====================================================================

### B1. Health (also wakes a sleeping Space)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# status "healthy"; services.ml_models true; services.models_loaded = the 4
# model names; services.transformers true;
# services.local_llm = { repo "unsloth/Qwen3.5-2B-GGUF", loaded true, error null };
# services.reasoning_llm "local" once that model has loaded (null while it is
# still loading or if it failed); services.reasoning_model "unsloth/Qwen3.5-2B-GGUF".
# If models_loaded lists fewer than 4, check the scikit-learn pin in
# hf_space_deploy/requirements.txt against the version the .pkl files were
# saved with.
# @name health
GET {{space}}/health

### B2. Transformer status
# Expect: HTTP 200
# transformers_available true; "loaded" is [] until the first BERT call
# (G1, I1 or J1), then ["url_phishing_bert"]; load_errors should stay {}.
# reasoning_llm.local = { repo, file, loaded true, loading false, error null }.
# @name v2Status
GET {{space}}/api/v2/status

### B3. Model registry
# Expect: HTTP 200
# total 4, loaded 4, every entry "source": "ml_model". Any entry showing
# "heuristic" means its .pkl failed to download from the model repo.
# @name modelsList
GET {{space}}/api/models/list

### B4. Model registry (alias route)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# Same body as B3.
# @name modelsAlias
GET {{space}}/models

### B5. OpenAPI schema (machine-readable list of every route)
# Expect: HTTP 200
# @name openapi
GET {{space}}/openapi.json

### B6. Gradio UI is mounted at /
# Expect: HTTP 200
# Returns the Gradio HTML page (notebooks, training, inference tabs).
# @name gradioUi
GET {{space}}/


# =====================================================================
# C. RAW MODEL PREDICTION — POST /api/models/predict
# =====================================================================
# Two ways to ask one model:
#   { "model_type": "...", "url": "https://..." }   the service computes the
#       model's features from the URL itself and the model answers (C13, C14).
#   { "model_type": "...", "input_data": { name: number, ... } }   features by
#       name. A model is only asked about a COMPLETE set of its own features.
# The retrained models take 39 (or 22) features, so the twelve original ones
#   url_length, hostname_length, path_length, is_https, has_ip_address,
#   has_suspicious_tld, subdomain_count, has_port, query_params_count,
#   has_at_symbol, has_double_slash, special_char_count
# are no longer enough on their own: C1-C6 and C10 now get the rule-based
# estimate ("inference_source": "heuristic") and a "missing_features" list.
# A value that is not a number is rejected with HTTP 400 (C11).

### C1. phishing_detection — the twelve original features, phishing-shaped
# Expect: HTTP 200
# The twelve original features are not a complete set for the retrained model,
# so the rule-based estimate answers: inference_source "heuristic", prediction 1,
# threat_score 0.55, reasons ["No HTTPS","IP address in URL"], and
# missing_features lists the model's 39 features. Send the URL instead (C13).
# @name predictPhishingThreat
POST {{space}}/api/models/predict
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "model_type": "phishing_detection",
  "input_data": {
    "url_length": 78, "hostname_length": 12, "path_length": 32, "is_https": 0,
    "has_ip_address": 1, "has_suspicious_tld": 0, "subdomain_count": 2,
    "has_port": 0, "query_params_count": 2, "has_at_symbol": 1,
    "has_double_slash": 0, "special_char_count": 6
  }
}

### C2. phishing_detection — the twelve original features, benign-shaped
# Expect: HTTP 200
# inference_source "heuristic", prediction 0, threat_score 0.0, reasons [],
# missing_features lists 39 names.
# @name predictPhishingBenign
POST {{space}}/api/models/predict
Content-Type: {{json}}

{
  "model_type": "phishing_detection",
  "input_data": {
    "url_length": 45, "hostname_length": 14, "path_length": 7, "is_https": 1,
    "has_ip_address": 0, "has_suspicious_tld": 0, "subdomain_count": 1,
    "has_port": 0, "query_params_count": 1, "has_at_symbol": 0,
    "has_double_slash": 0, "special_char_count": 3
  }
}

